From 7b30231b8a53008ce87bf9eab42584d4b3503050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 19:55:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00348/11171] [outer-loop] Fix P1 v2 eval crash (tuple-unpack)
 + add post-train checkpoint.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

v2 run completed all expensive work (12k train steps + 1500 decoder steps, nan=False)
then crashed at the eval sample-logging line: sc.ebt_descent_generate returns a tuple
(ids, n_eval) but the call wasn't unpacked, so gd was (list, int) and dec_ids choked
(TypeError: '>=' not supported between 'list' and 'int'). The crash also meant the
descent accuracy compared a tuple to a list (always False). One-line fix: gd, _ = ...

Also added a results/thesis_a_p1_v2_trained.pt checkpoint saved right after training +
decoder-fit, with a resume-guard that reloads and skips straight to eval if the ckpt
exists — so a future eval-stage crash can't cost another ~100min of training. CUDA was
healthy throughout (2 devices); this was a pure decode-formatting bug, not an eGPU fault.
Relaunched on cuda:1, conductor PAUSED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scripts/thesis_a_p1_discrete_search_v2.py | 25 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/thesis_a_p1_discrete_search_v2.py b/scripts/thesis_a_p1_discrete_search_v2.py
index 709c89895a..8545b55ba1 100644
--- a/scripts/thesis_a_p1_discrete_search_v2.py
+++ b/scripts/thesis_a_p1_discrete_search_v2.py
